      "text": "After Hours follows Paul Hackett, a mild-mannered word processor whose late-night venture into SoHo turns into a surreal nightmare. What begins as a promising encounter with the mysterious Marcy in a cafe spirals into an increasingly bizarre series of misadventures. As Paul attempts to return home, he faces a parade of eccentric characters and escalating obstacles: from missing money and mistaken identity to vigilante mobs and avant-garde artists. Each attempt to escape this downtown labyrinth only entangles him further, transforming Manhattan's streets into a kafka-esque maze where logic and reason gradually dissolve. The film masterfully builds tension through Paul's mounting desperation, as the ordinary world warps into something unrecognizable and threatening, with every potential savior becoming another source of danger."
